Two supported modes, both driven by the same shape of state:
1) Client-side mode: all rows are fetched once; TableState (search/filters/sort/page/pageSize) is applied via useMemo pipeline (filter -> search -> sort -> paginate) purely in the browser.
2) Server-side mode: TableState is serialized into query params sent to the API; the server returns { rows: T[], total: number } already filtered/sorted/paginated; the client just renders what it's given and total drives pagination controls.

TableState = {
  search: string;
  filters: Record<string, string | string[]>;
  sort: { columnKey: string; direction: 'asc' | 'desc' } | null;
  page: number;
  pageSize: number;
};
Source of truth for TableState is the URL (via useSearchParams / router query), not component state -- component state is just a derived read of the URL, and setters call router navigation (replace, not push, to avoid polluting history on every keystroke).
selectedIds: Set<string> -- lives in the parent (or a lifted state in DataTable via a controlled prop) since bulk actions are a parent concern; explicitly decide and document whether it resets on filter/page change.

